---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro'; import ColorIdentifier from '../components/ColorIdentifier.astro'; import JsonLd from '../components/JsonLd.astro';
const faq=[{q:'How do I identify a color from a photo?',a:'Upload an image, wait for it to appear, then select the point you want to sample. The tool reads that pixel and displays HEX, RGB and HSL values.'},{q:'Can I use my phone camera?',a:'Yes. Open this page over HTTPS in a supported browser, grant camera permission and use the live preview. You can also upload a photo instead.'},{q:'Will this tell me the exact factory paint code?',a:'No. It measures the visible color in the image. Factory paint codes are manufacturer-specific and should be verified using vehicle documentation or a trusted paint-code reference.'}];
const schema={'@context':'https://schema.org','@type':'SoftwareApplication',name:'ColorCode Identifier Color Scanner',applicationCategory:'MultimediaApplication',operatingSystem:'Any',description:'Sample a color from a camera or uploaded image and view HEX, RGB and HSL values.',offers:{'@type':'Offer',price:'0',priceCurrency:'USD'}};
---
<BaseLayout title="Color Identifier — Find a Color from Camera or Photo" description="Identify any visible color from a camera or uploaded image. Select a pixel to find its HEX, RGB, HSL values and closest color name."><JsonLd data={schema}/><div class="container"><div class="page-hero"><div class="breadcrumbs"><a href="/">Home</a> / Color Identifier</div><span class="eyebrow">Free online color tool</span><h1>Color Identifier from Camera or Photo</h1><p>Upload an image or use your camera, select the exact area you want to inspect, and discover its digital color values.</p></div><ColorIdentifier/><div class="content-layout"><article class="prose"><h2>How to identify a color</h2><ol><li>Choose <strong>Upload image</strong> or <strong>Use camera</strong>.</li><li>For camera use, allow browser permission when prompted.</li><li>Tap or click the area of the image you want to sample.</li><li>Read the HEX, RGB and HSL values shown in the result panel.</li><li>Copy the HEX value or collect additional samples in the swatch list.</li></ol><h2>What color formats do you get?</h2><p><strong>HEX</strong> is a six-digit hexadecimal notation commonly used in CSS and digital design. <strong>RGB</strong> represents red, green and blue channel values from 0 to 255. <strong>HSL</strong> describes hue, saturation and lightness in a more human-readable way.</p><h2>Can a camera identify the exact paint color?</h2><p>The tool can sample the visible pixel color in an image, but it cannot reliably determine a vehicle's original paint formula. Lighting, reflections, metallic finishes, camera processing and image compression affect the sampled result. Use an OEM paint code or a professional paint scanner when exact refinish matching is required.</p><h2>Related color tools</h2><ul><li><a href="/car-color-identifier/">Car color identifier</a></li><li><a href="/bike-color-identifier/">Bike color identifier</a></li><li><a href="/hex-to-rgb/">HEX to RGB converter</a></li><li><a href="/color-name-finder/">Color name finder</a></li><li><a href="/image-color-picker/">Image color picker</a></li></ul><h2>Frequently asked questions</h2><div class="faq-list">{faq.map(item=><details><summary>{item.q}</summary><p>{item.a}</p></details>)}</div></article><aside class="sidebar-card"><h3>Explore more</h3><a href="/car-color-identifier/">Car color identifier</a><a href="/bike-color-identifier/">Bike color identifier</a><a href="/color-palette-generator/">Palette generator</a><a href="/color-contrast-checker/">Contrast checker</a><a href="/blog/">Color guides</a></aside></div></div></BaseLayout>
